[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/2590/images/4082/4082-1780986518-1200256842.gif[/img][/center]
[url=https://falloutchatmod.com/]Fallout Chat Mod[/url] brings real-time community chat to Fallout 76 with a Pip-Boy-styled interface. Coordinate events, find trading partners, organize parties, and send private messages without switching away from your game. Choose how you want to use it:
[list]
[*][b]Desktop overlay:[/b] A transparent, draggable, resizable chat window that runs outside Fallout 76. Available for Windows and Linux.[/*]
[*][b]Optional in-game HUD mod:[/b] Display chat directly inside the game with HUDModLoader and either ZFE or xScal. One HUD download supports both extenders.[/*]
[/list]The desktop overlay does not modify game files, read game memory, inject code, or scan your network. It checks whether Fallout 76 is running to manage overlay visibility and does not require a script extender. The optional HUD mod is a separate installation that changes game UI assets. It uses your installed extender’s supported chat interface and information already exposed to the game’s HUD. The HUD mod and its dependencies may require updates after a Fallout 76 patch. Visit [url=https://falloutchatmod.com/]falloutchatmod.com[/url] for downloads, installation guides, and more information. You can report problems here on Nexus or through the application’s built-in bug and player reporting tools. 

[b][size=4]Code Signing and Virus Scanning[/size][/b] 
The Windows release installer is digitally signed. Release builds must pass launch smoke tests and a completed VirusTotal scan before publication. The v1.3.100 Windows installer completed its release scan with zero malicious or suspicious detections. [url=https://falloutchatmod.com/virustotal]View the current Windows installer VirusTotal report[/url]

[center][b][size=4]Main Features[/size][/b][/center]
[center][i]Infestation Chat[/i][/center]
[center] [img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/2590/images/4082/4082-1780986682-344970336.gif[/img] [/center]
[center][i]Party Up[/i][/center]
[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/2590/images/4082/4082-1780986698-180659483.gif[/img] [/center]
[center][i]Fallout 76 Wiki Built In[/i][/center]
[center] [img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/2590/images/4082/4082-1780986806-1247131354.gif[/img] [/center]
[center][i]Custom Commands[/i][/center]
[center] [img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/2590/images/4082/4082-1780986668-546220891.gif[/img][/center]
[list]
[*][b]Community channels:[/b] General, Trading, Events, Infests, and Raids, with channel labels and quick shortcuts such as /g, /t, /e, /i, and /r.[/*]
[*][b]Private messaging:[/b] Find other users and exchange direct messages with conversation history and unread indicators. Private conversations remain separate from public channel messages and mentions.[/*]
[*][b]Party chat:[/b] Create public or private parties to organize activities and keep your group connected.[/*]
[*][b]Two-way Discord bridge:[/b] Supported community-channel messages travel between Fallout Chat Mod and Discord, keeping players connected whether they are in-game or browsing Discord.[/*]
[*][b]Steam or Discord sign-in:[/b] Create an account and link your chat session using either provider. Steam sign-in does not require linking Discord. You can add Discord later from your website profile.[/*]
[*][b]Display names:[/b] Choose a custom display name, or use your Steam display name when signing in through Steam without entering one.[/*]
[*][b]Optional server chat:[/b] The HUD’s SERVER channel connects players assigned to the same confirmed game-world room. Messages from your current server also appear in General with a SERVER label. Leaving a world clears the previous room’s state.[/*]
[*][b]Custom emojis and GIFs:[/b] The desktop overlay includes a server-emoji picker and Tenor GIF search. The HUD renders bundled Unicode and known custom emoji as static pictures, with readable :name: fallbacks for unsupported custom emoji. It does not load remote image/GIF attachments or play animated emoji.[/*]
[*][b]Built-in wiki and commands:[/b] Look up Fallout 76 information and use chat commands without opening a separate browser window.[/*]
[*][b]Community giveaways:[/b] Start an item raffle with /giveaway start, let other players join, and have a winner selected when the timer ends. Use /giveaway list to check active giveaways.[/*]
[*][b]Appearance settings:[/b] Customize the desktop overlay’s theme, name colors, and chat appearance. Supporter benefits include additional cosmetic options.[/*]
[*][b]Moderation and reporting:[/b] Built-in player and bug reports, plus a browser-based moderation portal with moderation actions, evidence, audit logs, automated filters, and role-based access.[/*]
[*][b]Manual updates:[/b] The overlay notifies you when a newer version is available. Updates are downloaded and installed manually; the application does not automatically download or install them.[/*]
[/list][b][size=4]What’s New in v1.3.100[/size][/b]
[list]
[*]Steam and Discord sign-in across website account creation, desktop onboarding, and HUD account linking.[/*]
[*]Steam display-name fallback and the option to link Discord later.[/*]
[*]Fixed public server-feed messages appearing in the PM view after switching tabs.[/*]
[*]Improved HUD send routing, authentication, reconnects, and message-history recovery when leaving and joining worlds.[/*]
[*]Improved server-room handling and added current-server messages to General.[/*]
[*]Improved Page Up/Page Down channel navigation and xScal input handling.[/*]
[*]Added HUD input handoff safeguards when opening the PipBoy.[/*]
[*]Improved overlay dragging, name effects, and restoration of supporter benefits from Discord roles.[/*]
[*]Unified the HUD download: one auto-detecting mod file with both ZFE and xScal configuration examples.[/*]
[/list][b][size=4]Requirements — Desktop Overlay[/size][/b]
[list]
[*]Fallout 76 on PC.[/*]
[*]64-bit Windows 10 or Windows 11, or a compatible Linux desktop environment.[/*]
[*]An internet connection.[/*]
[*]A Steam or Discord account. Discord sign-in also requires membership in the Fallout Chat Mod Discord server.[/*]
[*]Borderless Windowed mode for the desktop overlay. Linux compositor-specific setup instructions are available on the website.[/*]
[*]No script extender or HUD mod is required for the desktop overlay.[/*]
[/list][b][size=4]Desktop Overlay Installation[/size][/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download the latest Windows installer or Linux package from the Files tab or [url=https://falloutchatmod.com/]falloutchatmod.com[/url].[/*]
[*][b]Windows:[/b] Extract the Windows ZIP and run the included Fallout Chat Mod Setup installer. It installs for your user account.[/*]
[*][b]Linux:[/b] Make the AppImage executable and run it, or install the .deb package on a compatible Debian/Ubuntu-based distribution. The Linux ZIP includes installation documentation.[/*]
[*]Launch Fallout Chat Mod and sign in with Steam or Discord.[/*]
[*]Complete onboarding and choose your appearance settings. Enter a custom display name if desired; Steam users can leave it blank to use their Steam display name.[/*]
[*]Set Fallout 76 to Borderless Windowed mode and launch the game. Follow the website’s additional setup guidance for your Linux desktop if needed.[/*]
[*]Press Insert to focus chat. The default desktop hide shortcut is Delete, and Page Up/Page Down cycle channels. Keybinds can be changed in Settings.[/*]
[/list]To update, download the latest package and run the installer or install the newer Linux package. Your existing user settings are stored separately from the application files. 

[b][size=4]Optional In-Game HUD Mod[/size][/b]
The separate HUD ZIP needs HUDModLoader and either ZFE or xScal. It does not need the desktop overlay. The ZIP root [code]README.txt[/code] explains the two folders; choose only the extender you installed.
[list]
[*][code]ZFE (Install for ZFE only)/[/code]: [code]Data (drag the contents into data folder)/[/code] holds the BA2, FCM INI, loader INI, and ZFE fragment.[/*]
[*][code]xScal (Install for xScal only)/[/code]: the same labeled Data folder, plus [code]xscal.ini[/code] beside it.[/*]
[/list]Each folder also has [code]INSTALL.txt[/code] and a root [code]Fallout76Custom.ini[/code] merge template. The loader file includes HUDModLoader's default entries plus FCMChatWidget. [b]Merge shared INIs; never overwrite an existing one.[/b] No separate [code]zfe.ini[/code] is required.

[b]Install[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Close Fallout 76. Install HUDModLoader and one extender. Extract the HUD ZIP outside the game and open the matching provider folder.[/*]
[*]Open the selected [code]Data (drag the contents into data folder)/[/code] folder and drag its contents into the game's [code]Data/[/code] folder, not the labeled folder itself. Skip existing INIs; keep edits.[/*]
[*]If the game's [code]Data/hudmodloader.ini[/code] is missing, copy the packaged file (HUDModLoader defaults plus FCMChatWidget). Otherwise add [code]FCMChatWidget[/code] once and preserve existing entries. For a manual BA2 install, append [code]FCMChatWidget.ba2[/code] once to [code]sResourceArchive2List[/code] in your Documents [code]Fallout76Custom.ini[/code].[/*]
[*]For xScal, merge the packaged [code]xscal.ini[/code] [code][Chat][/code] keys into [code]xscal.ini[/code] beside [code]Fallout76.exe[/code]: [code]enabled=true[/code] and [code]relayEndpoint=wss://falloutchatmod.com/relay[/code]. ZFE uses the packaged fragment in its Data path.[/*]
[*]Restart the game, open the F11 FCM menu, and enter the displayed link code at [url=https://falloutchatmod.com/link]falloutchatmod.com/link[/url].[/*]
[/list]
Quick Configuration 2 and NukaMods users: import only the selected folder's [code]Data (drag the contents into data folder)/FCMChatWidget.ba2[/code], then follow the remaining INI steps. Let the manager maintain the archive-list entry. Do not import the combined ZIP. On updates, replace only the BA2 and keep edited INIs. Verify one deployed BA2 and one archive entry.

[b][size=4]HUD Controls[/size][/b]
[list]
[*]Insert opens chat input.[/*]
[*]Enter sends your message; Escape cancels input.[/*]
[*]Page Up/Page Down switch channels.[/*]
[*]While a typing session is open, the configurable [code]scrollUpKey[/code] / [code]scrollDownKey[/code] bindings scroll the feed (Arrow Up/Down by default). [code]scrollBottomKey[/code] is unbound by default; assign Home, End, F12, or a forwarded action in [code]Data/FCMChat.ini[/code] if you want a keyboard shortcut for newest. The F11 menu always includes Scroll to newest.[/*]
[*]Use /g, /t, /e, /i, or /r to route a message to a community channel.[/*]
[*]Use /s or /server after the current server/world session has been confirmed.[/*]
[*]Use /hide to hide the feed and Insert to restore it.[/*]
[*]Press F11 to open HUDModLoader and find the FCM customization menu.[/*]
[/list]Server-room detection depends on information available to the HUD and may take time after joining a world. Please report cases where players in the same world do not share a SERVER room, or where a room fails to clear after leaving. 

[b][size=4]Roadmap[/size][/b] 
Longer-term ideas include:
[list]
[*]Clans with shared chat and management tools.[/*]
[*]Additional game support, including Fallout 3, New Vegas, and Fallout 4.[/*]
[*]More trading and community-tool integrations.[/*]
[*]Additional account-linking options, including Nexus.[/*]
[/list]Private messaging, custom name colors, Steam/Discord linking, and the optional HUD/server-chat features are now available rather than roadmap-only items. 

[b][size=4]Support and Bug Reports[/size][/b] 
Use the application’s built-in reporting tools, post in the Nexus discussion or bug sections, or join our Discord: [url=https://discord.gg/NJBJqyvRJC]Join the Fallout Chat Mod Discord[/url] For installation guides and the latest downloads: [url=https://falloutchatmod.com/]falloutchatmod.com[/url] When reporting a problem, include your operating system, application/HUD version, and whether you use the desktop overlay, ZFE HUD, or xScal HUD. For server-chat issues, include whether you were on a public or private world and whether the problem occurred after leaving or joining a server.
